# ============================================================
# .gitignore for structure-negative-steering
# ============================================================

# ----- Experiments — results are HPC-only, test DEFINITIONS are tracked -----
# The experiments/ tree (prior runs migrated from the HPC scratch folder plus
# future run outputs) is local/HPC-only. The one exception that IS tracked is
# each target's test spec, config.yml. Derived inputs/ and run/ outputs stay
# ignored even under benchmarking/.
# Documentation lives in the root README.md, not in per-directory READMEs.
# The tree is experiments/benchmarking/<unconstrained|constrained>/<TARGET>/.
#
# No *.pdb is tracked anywhere under experiments/. The eighteen reference
# complexes live once in data/reference_complexes/ and every config in every
# tree points back at that copy, so no two arms can disagree about truth.
experiments/*
!experiments/benchmarking/
experiments/benchmarking/*
!experiments/benchmarking/*/
experiments/benchmarking/*/*
!experiments/benchmarking/*/*/
experiments/benchmarking/*/*/*
!experiments/benchmarking/*/*/config.yml

# The dose sweep is generated by scripts/make_dose_sweep.py from those specs.
# Its configs are tracked for the same reason, the run outputs are not. It
# carries no *.pdb of its own. Each config points back at data/.
!experiments/dose-sweep/
experiments/dose-sweep/*
!experiments/dose-sweep/*/
experiments/dose-sweep/*/*
!experiments/dose-sweep/*/*/
experiments/dose-sweep/*/*/*
!experiments/dose-sweep/*/*/config.yml

# The interface-ablation controls are generated by
# scripts/make_ablation_controls.py. Same rule again, configs tracked and run
# outputs not, plus one shared copy of each reference structure. This tree is
# deliberately outside experiments/benchmarking/ so no benchmark run can be
# overwritten by a control run.
!experiments/interface-ablation/
experiments/interface-ablation/*
!experiments/interface-ablation/*/
experiments/interface-ablation/*/*
!experiments/interface-ablation/*/*/
experiments/interface-ablation/*/*/*
!experiments/interface-ablation/*/*/config.yml

# ----- Nextflow -----
.nextflow/
.nextflow.log*
.nextflow.history*
.nextflow-reports/
work/
nxf_home/

# ----- Pipeline-style outputs -----
*_results/
results/

# ----- SLURM logs -----
*.out
*.err
slurm-*.out
slurm-*.err

# ----- Python -----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ----- Jupyter -----
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ----- macOS -----
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*

# ----- Microsoft Office lock files -----
~$*

# ----- Editors / IDEs / agents -----
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ----- Environment / secrets -----
.env
.env.local
*.local

# ----- Smoke-run outputs. The config is tracked, the run is not -----
tests/smoke/run/
tests/smoke/run_cli/
tests/smoke/.cli_view*
tests/smoke/inputs/
tests/smoke/*.out
tests/smoke/*.err

# ----- Workflow-check outputs. Same rule: the config is tracked, the run is not -----
tests/test_run/run/
tests/test_run/run_cli/
tests/test_run/inputs/
tests/test_run/*.out
tests/test_run/*.err

# ----- Coverage artefacts, regenerated by any test run -----
htmlcov/
lcov.info
.coverage
# Written by the --cov-report=xml the Tests workflow passes, and uploaded to
# Codecov from there rather than committed.
coverage.xml

# ----- Build / packaging -----
build/
dist/
*.egg
.eggs/

# ----- Singularity / Apptainer images -----
*.img
*.sif

# ----- Sync helper artefacts -----
rsync_dryrun*.txt
rsync_deletions*.txt

# ----- Quarto render artifacts (figures/ PNGs+SVGs are committed separately) -----
*_files/
analysis/**/*.html

# ----- Nextflow run reports, regenerated on every run -----
trace.txt
report.html
timeline.html

# ----- Archive: superseded code kept for the record, not run -----
# archive/prerepo_scripts/ holds the pre-repo sequence-walk and seed-variance
# diagnostics. Nothing imports them and they are excluded from ruff. Kept
# because eight of them have no descendant anywhere in this repo's history.
archive/

# The testing image's def is local-only. The image it builds is installed
# under the regular boltz2_negsteer.img name on the HPC, so publishing this
# would only confuse anyone building from containers/boltz2_negsteer.def.
containers/boltz2_negsteer_testing.def

# ----- Working notes, local only -----
notes/repo-cleanup-playbook.md
docs/development_notes/

# ----- OS / misc -----
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Scratch frame from docs/make_logo.py, removed on a clean run.
docs/.logo_tmp.png
